Google Cloud Agent Platform — Services


|  # | Service                    | Simple Meaning                 | What you use it for                                                 |
| -: | -------------------------- | ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |
|  1 | **Model Garden**           | Collection of AI models        | Find and use models such as **Gemma, Gemini and other models**      |
|  2 | **Tuning**                 | Customize an AI model          | Fine-tune/adapt a model for a specific task                         |
|  3 | **Evaluation**             | Test AI quality                | Check whether your AI model/agent gives good answers                |
|  4 | **Model Registry**         | Model storage/catalog          | Manage and track your AI/ML models                                  |
|  5 | **Endpoints**              | AI model access point          | Deploy a model so applications can send requests to it              |
|  6 | **Batch Inference**        | Process many requests together | Generate predictions for a large amount of data                     |
|  7 | **Provisioned Throughput** | Reserved AI capacity           | Get predictable AI processing capacity for production               |
|  8 | **Datasets**               | Store/manage training data     | Prepare and manage datasets for AI/ML                               |
|  9 | **Feature Store**          | Store ML features              | Store and reuse important input features for ML models              |
| 10 | **Experiments**            | Track ML experiments           | Compare different models, parameters and results                    |
| 11 | **Training**               | Train ML models                | Build/train machine-learning models                                 |
| 12 | **Ray on Agent Platform**  | Distributed AI/ML computing    | Run scalable Python/AI workloads using Ray                          |
| 13 | **Pipelines**              | Automate ML workflows          | Connect steps such as data → training → evaluation → deployment     |
| 14 | **Metadata**               | Track ML information           | Keep information about datasets, models, runs and pipelines         |
| 15 | **Monitoring**             | Watch deployed AI systems      | Monitor performance, errors and changes in production               |
| 16 | **Get API key**            | Get an API key                 | Allow applications to communicate with supported Google AI services |
| 17 | **Tutorials**              | Learning resources             | Follow Google Cloud tutorials and hands-on examples                 |


