Easy way to remember the whole flow

Think of building an AI application like building a student:

| Stage                | Google Cloud service         | Student example                      |
| -------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| 📚 Find a model      | **Model Garden**             | Choose a teacher/book                |
| 🎯 Customize         | **Tuning**                   | Teach the student a specific subject |
| 📝 Test              | **Evaluation**               | Conduct an exam                      |
| 🗂️ Store model      | **Model Registry**           | Keep the student's records           |
| 🚀 Deploy            | **Endpoints**                | Student starts working               |
| 📊 Monitor           | **Monitoring**               | Check performance                    |
| 🔄 Improve           | **Experiments / Training**   | Practice and improve                 |
| ⚙️ Automate          | **Pipelines**                | Create an automatic study process    |
| 💾 Manage data       | **Datasets / Feature Store** | Manage study materials               |
| 🧾 Track information | **Metadata**                 | Maintain records                     |


==========

Model Garden → Evaluation → Endpoints → Monitoring → Pipelines

And for your Agentic AI / RAG projects:

Model → RAG/Data → Agent → Evaluation → Deployment → Monitoring

This will give you a strong practical understanding of the Google Cloud AI workflow.


